	(text "Our adapter: a GND between VOUT and VCLK, short runs away from the\nstepper wires, decoupling on VDD at the sensor, never hot-plugged.\nLight: two fibers on the connector's optical port (an LED, planned)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 345.44 251.46 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "616c40ed-bcec-4cff-870b-8850749dc9bc")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 340.36 218.44)
		(end 477.52 269.24)
		(stroke
			(width 0.254)
			(type solid)
			(color 72 72 72 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(uuid "155bb0e0-6d90-49fb-a929-4358f0373c98")
	)
	(text "Endoscope camera"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 341.63 219.71 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d56f27e9-1639-48d8-9c8e-ac530894d16b")
	)
	(text "THE FFC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 287.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "061f43ee-f7b0-4b9c-affe-cbd3ec43832a")
	)
	(text "Pin = the breakouts' printed numbers, the same on both ends:\n1 GND (guard), 2 E+, 3-4 S+/S-, 5 E-, 6 GND, 7 ENDSTOP_K,\n8 GND, 9-10 D+/D-, 11 GND, 12 TOOL_ID, 13-15 +5V_TOOL,\n16 GND, 17-20 K (A1 A2 B1 B2). 0.5 mm FFC: ~0.5 A a contact,\nso 1.5 A on 13-15: the tool gets 1 A (F1001).\nCheck 1 -> 1 with a meter before power: reversed, 13-15 land\non 6-8."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 292.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a57a3a37-d05c-4895-9f55-165a640b404d")
	)
	(text "THE TOOLS (THE ID ON THE SCREW AND THE POGO)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 152.4 287.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e90afe93-afa8-4063-9de1-8849ce6aba67")
	)
	(text "Simple: GND and the ID bridged (copper tape, a\ntemplate): there, never powered; the RFID tag says which.\nPassive: a resistor GND-ID, powered, no link.\nActuator: a resistor >= 4.7k, powered, the half-duplex link\n(pings; lost = gone). USB: as an actuator, D+/D- pads.\nA resistor on the screws or on the pogos, never a bridge\non one and a resistor on the other. High power: tethered,\nits 5 V screw open (GND kept)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 152.4 292.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f2aa3405-c4fd-40e8-9f6d-771e81012368")
	)
	(text "THE TOOL 5 V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 297.18 287.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "280efb0d-6b6c-47e4-9f35-f21487c133f2")
	)
	(text "Read the ID with the 5 V off, then switch it on (GP9, the\nhub board's U1006 + F1001 1 A); off before undocking.\nA tool with a chip on the ID line keeps it high-Z while\nunpowered (74LVC2G07 / a 2N7002): else the line clamps\nat ~0.6 V and reads as a low band. USB pins: fine."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 297.18 292.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "de326b21-a230-42ec-b576-e395b53d1b24")
	)
	(text "THE DRAG CHAIN"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 424.18 287.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c2c4e8a6-d0eb-469c-a196-10f0d9b5535c")
	)
	(text "Toolchanger: the USB-C cable, CAT6, the K ribbon.\nThe axis: Z (4), the Y/Z endstops, the MPU9250\n(I2C + 3V3 + GND), the endoscope's USB.\nEvery cable anchored on the fixed side (HS) first;\nacross the cell only the FFC (a slack U-loop)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 424.18 292.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a1f2c189-cf61-4529-bd4c-2066d386cafd")
	)
